   },
   "description": "Time from case open to the FIRST staff reply, with time spent awaiting the customer already subtracted — so this is our latency, not theirs. The sold targets are 2 business days (standard), the next business day (priority) and 8 hours any day of the week (premium). Only premium's is directly comparable to this chart: it is wall-clock with no business-hours exemption, so p90 crossing 8h IS a breach and the alert fires at 6h. The other two are business-day targets, which a wall-clock quantile cannot express — a priority case raised at 17:01 on a Friday is not late until Monday evening, about 79 hours later — so read those two as queue health rather than compliance."
