   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "unit": "ops"
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "legend": {
     "displayMode": "list",
     "placement": "bottom",
     "showLegend": true
    },
    "tooltip": {
     "mode": "multi",
     "sort": "desc"
    }
   },
   "description": "opened = a case exists. unentitled = the sending org has no designated contact OF ITS OWN (the allowance pools subtree-wide, ownership does not), so the message landed without a case — normal for an org with no add-on, a product signal in volume. open_failed = the message committed and its case row did not, which is always a bug: the tenant saw success and will never get a case number. severity_downgraded = an org below premium asked for urgent severity and the case was opened as high instead. Not a fault: urgent is admitted only at premium, so every increment is a customer asking for the one thing that level alone sells, which makes this the most direct read on premium's unmet demand the system produces. over_allowance = the account's case volume in the rolling window has passed what its CONTACT COUNT entitles it to. Not a fault and never a refusal: the per-contact price assumes contacts proxy for case volume, which holds at ten seats and fails at a hundred where three named contacts become an internal help desk forwarding tickets. A sustained rate here is a commercial conversation, not an incident."
  },
